+### Native activity decoration
+
+`ctx.ui.registerActivityDecoration(factory, overrides?)` attaches presentation to the existing foreground status, without replacing the editor. It returns an idempotent removal function, or `undefined` when unavailable or declined. Register during `session_start`; removal, reload, session replacement, and shutdown dispose the controller exactly once. This API requires the source host containing these hooks; unmodified releases do not provide it. Do not fall back to editor replacement.
+
+The factory runs only on an eligible interactive TTY with a supported native editor/status renderer. Print, JSON, RPC, and redirected/non-TTY modes never invoke it. Competing registrations and unsupported custom editors remain intact, with one diagnostic. `CustomEditor` supplies `supportsActivityDecoration: true`; subclasses must preserve the native status rendering and width-priority contract to retain that opt-in. Other renderers are declined unless they explicitly implement the same contract and opt in.
+
+The exported `ActivityDecorationController` receives a synchronous initial and current `ActivityDecorationSnapshot` plus a scoped update function. Snapshots contain only opaque `runId`, `ownerGeneration`, native `kind`, producer-derived `genericWorking`, `eligible`, `visible`, `waiting`, and normalized readonly `preferences`; no prompts, model identifiers, or conversation data. `ActivityIndicatorPreferences` contains `enabled`, `text`, `animation`, `randomTiming`, `color`, `motion`, `ascii`, `showElapsed`, `showAction`, and `showOutputTokens` (see [Settings](settings.md#activity-indicator)). Preferences refresh the same controller through a new scoped update handle, without recreating its run/word selector. Animation/color changes alone must not reset a word deadline.
+
+Optional `ActivityDecorationOverrides` is bounded to `{ enabled?: false, motion?: "normal" | "reduced" | "plain", ascii?: boolean }`. Pass only explicitly supplied invocation controls; absent fields inherit saved preferences. Overrides never persist. `{ enabled: false }` reserves a dormant, revocable registration without invoking the factory, changing native presentation, or allocating feature resources. Its idempotent removal/reset/shutdown constructs/disposes no controller; saved settings cannot enable this invocation. Ineligible/noninteractive registration remains a no-op, even with overrides. Use state, not callback counts. The run identity survives phase replacement and intermediate `agent_end`; final settlement or the end of standalone native work clears it. `visible` follows the native status surface and terminal visibility policy, not extension tool events.
+
+Updates accept only `{ label?, reservedWidth?, nativeTextFallback?: true, glyph: "animated" | "static" | "hidden" }`. Supply a complete single-line label including punctuation and a terminal-cell reservation large enough for it. Only producer-marked generic Working may be replaced: Whimsical shows the complete word, Operational native text, Both both. Custom Working messages (even spelled `Working`), retry, compaction and summary retain real text/semantic colors without appended words. `genericWorking` changes synchronously at `setWorkingMessage`, including explicit messages spelled `Working`; it contains no text. Defer a first bank draw until a word-renderable generic phase, without inventing a wait/run or restarting an already-earned display delay. Keep already selected same-run words/deadlines through meaningful phases. Omit `label` before its first usable display. For invalid-bank provenance, omit `label` and send `nativeTextFallback: true` after the display delay: Whimsical/Both format generic native `Working…` (`Working...` in ASCII), while Operational/Plain remain literal. No message-spelling inference is used. Cancellation/overflow hints take precedence: the complete decoration is omitted and native Working restored before native text is truncated. Both editor-border and standalone status paths use the same native object. Glyph preferences control only the current native Loader. The host owns the ten local presets, stable frame widths, Random run choice and optional 8-second visible-busy switching deadline independently of words. Reduced freezes the representative preset; Plain is literal native text. Waiting/hidden/idle states cancel switching; same-run resume retains the preset with a fresh interval. Theme accent resolves each render; Claude applies the documented terracotta only to ordinary decoration. Explicit `setWorkingIndicator` frames/colors remain authoritative. No second busy animation is created. Normal elapsed refresh reuses native redraws; static/Reduced presentation can own one scoped one-second callback, never allocated by rendering. Removal restores current native settings without resetting retry countdowns.
+
+Foreground metadata remains host-only, never part of controller snapshots or updates. NativeActivityDecoration captures the monotonic origin with its existing retained run identity. InteractiveMode observes only scalar tool names/ids and assistant `usage.output` from its main AgentSession subscription; it forwards no content/arguments/results to presentation selection. `parentToolCallId` identifies nested tools, which remain represented by their parent. Children/background agents are not subscribed to this main session UI; summary/compaction usage is not a main assistant response. Public message events have no stable response/run id and start/update objects differ: the host uses the producer's serialized message_start/update/end lifetime with a scoped response token, replacing snapshots and finalizing once, including reported failed attempts. Observation occurs synchronously before UI initialization can yield; reset/session replacement revokes queued old handling and subscription ownership. Unknown tool finishes and revoked response handles are ignored. These events cannot distinguish arbitrary injected untagged old starts; provenance is the trusted current main-session subscription, not guessed ids or message timestamps. No event/provider/protocol schema is changed. Metadata observations do not notify the word controller or reset word/preset deadlines. See settings for reported-subtotal limitations and width omission order.
+
+Before waits become usable, the host hides decoration and stops its glyph. Waits come from synchronous runner prompt depth and actual native input lifetimes, including asynchronous custom factories and hidden/noncapturing overlays. A controller must cancel its own scheduled work on waiting/hidden/idle snapshots and dispose, retaining any same-run label locally for resume. Updates from an obsolete snapshot, status owner, or removed registration return `false`; never use them to restore host visibility or acquire a foreground surface. Rendering must not schedule work or select labels.
+
+```typescript
+const remove = ctx.ui.registerActivityDecoration(() => ({
+  onSnapshot(state, update) {
+    // A real controller owns its delay/rotation callbacks and cancels them on suppression.
+    if (state.visible) update({ label: "Working…", reservedWidth: 14, glyph: "static" });
+  },
+  dispose() {
+    // Cancel this controller's owned callbacks/subscriptions only.
+  },
+}));
+// On disable/unload:
+remove?.();
+```
