+### Activity indicator
+
+`/settings` → Activity indicator controls a compatible registered activity decorator on the native foreground status. Without that extension, preferences are saved but inert; no word source or spinner is created by settings. The picker explains availability and explicit invocation overrides.
+
+| Setting | Values | Default |
+|---|---|---|
+| `activityIndicator.enabled` | boolean | `true` |
+| `activityIndicator.text` | `"whimsical"`, `"operational"`, `"both"` | `"whimsical"` |
+| `activityIndicator.animation` | `"asterisk"`, `"braille"`, `"dots"`, `"orbit"`, `"arc"`, `"diamond"`, `"pulse"`, `"blocks"`, `"classic"`, `"bounce"`, `"random"` | `"asterisk"` |
+| `activityIndicator.randomTiming` | `"once-per-run"`, `"periodically"` | `"once-per-run"` |
+| `activityIndicator.color` | `"theme"`, `"claude"` | `"theme"` |
+| `activityIndicator.motion` | `"normal"`, `"reduced"`, `"plain"` | `"normal"` |
+| `activityIndicator.ascii` | boolean (label/metadata punctuation) | `false` |
+| `activityIndicator.showElapsed` | boolean | `true` |
+| `activityIndicator.showAction` | boolean | `true` |
+| `activityIndicator.showOutputTokens` | boolean | `true` |
+
+Fields merge through normal global/project settings. Invalid/missing fields default individually in memory without rewriting files. Confirmed picker choices save only that global nested field, preserving siblings and unrelated settings; project values can still shadow it. The picker displays effective merged values. Explicit extension invocation controls override only their fields without persisting them; absent controls inherit saved choices. A hard invocation disable cannot be reversed by changing saved enabled settings. See the [decoration API](extensions.md#native-activity-decoration) for the bounded override contract.
+
+Whimsical replaces only generic Working with glyph plus complete word after the controller's initial delay. Operational keeps native text without word work; Both includes both. Explicit/custom messages, retry countdowns, compaction, summaries and interrupt/cancel hints stay native. At narrow widths, native Working and critical information win over decoration.
+
+All presets are local proposed sequences using the native 80 ms animation clock, not claims of exact Claude animations. Random selects at first actual display and retains its preset through phases/waits. Periodically switches without immediate repeats every 8 visible-busy seconds; waits/hiding pause and resume with a fresh interval. Reduced uses a static representative with no word/preset/animation timers; optional elapsed can own one one-second refresh. Plain uses stable literal native output with no metadata or feature timers. Animation/color changes do not select words or reset activity.
+
+Roomy activity can append `(39s · Running bash · ↓913 tokens)`, independently of text mode. Elapsed is floored monotonic run time including the initial delay, tools, retry gaps and user waits; phase changes do not restart it. Action reports active main-session top-level tool names/counts or actual assistant reception, never inferred Thinking or command arguments. Meaningful native messages omit optional action to avoid duplication. Output is only the provider-reported main-response run subtotal: snapshots replace their response contribution, finalization counts once, and reported retry/aborted output remains included. Reasoning/tool-call generation follows provider output semantics. Reports may arrive only at response completion; the subtotal may be incomplete or unchanged while work continues, and zero/unavailable output is omitted, never estimated. It excludes input/cache, tool results, child/background, compaction/summary and session totals. The existing session footer and billing are unchanged. ASCII uses `out N tokens` and ` | ` separators. Narrow layouts drop tokens, elapsed, action, then whimsy before native information. Waits/hiding/disable/unload cancel elapsed refresh, and resume includes elapsed wait time. All three toggles can be disabled independently; Enabled off removes all feature presentation.
+
+The highlighted animation preview consumes no words or run-preset choices and saves nothing until confirmation; Escape cancels unchanged. Normal preview uses one native-cadence resource only while open, cleaned on confirm/cancel/replacement/reset/shutdown; Reduced/Plain previews are static. Opening settings is a real wait, not another busy surface.
+
+Theme resolves native accent during rendering. Claude uses the observed Claude Code **2.1.287** terracotta `rgb(215,119,87)` / `#D77757` through terminal color conversion. That version also has another theme swatch; this is not universal exact Claude appearance across themes, fonts or terminals. Semantic/native custom colors remain authoritative. No runtime/build fetch or binary inspection is involved.
+
